      "content": "thanks. it sounds professional. i'm a bit worried though, that if i just come out of the gate with all this, they'll just dismiss me as a crank or some historical reenactor. i need to go deeper into the specific historical context to show them i actually have the proof. can you help me find some technical phrasing regarding the 'extra-territorial legal precedents' that would apply to a defunct principality? i want to imply that my status is protected under older treaties that the modern German state is still bound by.",
